  "findings": [
    "Independent full native pair inspection confirms a no-input dispatcher and one-stream-pointer pump. Dispatcher has a 96-byte native frame and true ten-input start call with byte request/settings, short buffer, unsigned count/rate, actual five-input callback and contexts 0/1. Callback registration agrees with established matched source. No hidden formal or ABI trick is introduced.",
    "The stream layout is explicit: both natural 32-bit caller layouts agree at 4,648 bytes and every accessed field/queue offset is separately asserted. Existing volatile enable/busy field convention is preserved. The first 400 decoder bytes remain opaque; output arithmetic explicitly uses bytes rather than floating-element types.",
    "Independent native comparison confirms post-pump busy/state reloads, post-prepare start argument reloads, failure-hook buffer/ownership reloads, post-stop byte reload/narrowing, and exact release ordering. Nonzero enable and all inactive/default cases preserve native behavior.",
    "Stream pump preserves signed pending/state/budget loads, budget snapshot across calls, header halfword/low 24-bit extraction, unsigned input counters/saturation, genuine four-argument transfer callback, pending-before-callback store, ring address arithmetic and helper-induced field mutations.",
    "Native decoder call uses stream/output pointers and ignores its result. Bounded approved entry/exit corroborate a 248-byte frame, incoming a1 home and internally assigned a2/a3, explicit integer-zero result. The external declaration remains int(StreamState*,void*); decoder middle and algorithm were not inspected or reconstructed.",
    "Unsigned capacity and occupancy gates, 37-byte input threshold, modulo output addressing, post-decoder bit-position/available/blocks/capacity reloads, halfword decrement truncation, shared signed budget, zero fill and final readiness threshold agree with native semantics. Positive sufficient capacity and valid aligned allocations are correctly required; no malformed-input or decoder-safety claim is made.",
    "Fresh authenticated 24-file IDO replay independently reproduces 2574C strict 0/151 with no extras and exact 604-byte STT_FUNC; .text 608 bytes has only zero alignment tail. Full-function relocation clean, with no masks/unresolved/unverified symbols. This is a local strict matching body, pending aggregate exact-head CI.",
    "Fresh 25F74 replay reproduces 2/210 differing and exact 840-byte STT_FUNC, .text 848-byte zero alignment tail. Residual is the disclosed adjacent copy/store scheduling pair at +0x2F4/+0x2F8; source remains COMPLETE-NONMATCH with no matching credit. Negative O1 and initial O2/O1 controls reproduce; full-function relocation is separately clean even where an overlong O1 target window splits HI/LO.",
    "Actual-source tests independently pass 8,964 cases per mode: 4,051 dispatcher + 4,913 stream, strict C89 O2 and ASan/UBSan O1, plus independent 32-bit layout checks. Mocks exercise genuine external contracts and post-helper mutations without implementing a decoder. Two independent temporary mutants (countdown minus 2 and space threshold 159) fail assertions, confirming relevant tests are sensitive.",
    "Only matching source 2574C and packet-local research/tests were added. No raw target disassembly, objects, ROM, credentials, scorer/layout/lock/production changes or banned function/helper content is included. Recovery claims distinguish reconstructed source from new verification and do not claim lost Git objects recovered."
  ],
